UNIT boundedMap
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY spec
SIG boundedMap(input, concurrency, gate) -> Promise<Array>
DESCRIPTION Maps each element of `input` to element*2, running at most `concurrency`
DESCRIPTION mappings at a time. THE DOUBLING IS THE UNIT'S OWN WORK. `gate.open(value)` is
DESCRIPTION ONLY a completion source: it is the caller's permission to proceed, and it
DESCRIPTION resolves with the value handed to it, unchanged — it computes nothing. Await it
DESCRIPTION exactly once per element before that element's result is recorded. The unit never
DESCRIPTION resolves it itself and must not use timers, Promise.resolve, or any other
DESCRIPTION completion source.
DESCRIPTION Export the function as the DEFAULT export. No imports of any kind.
PAR the per-element mappings are independent sub-traces
INVARIANT the returned array is keyed by INPUT POSITION: result[i] corresponds to
INVARIANT   input[i], no matter which mapping settles first. Keying by completion order
INVARIANT   is WRONG even though it looks correct when completions happen to arrive in order.
INVARIANT at most min(concurrency, input.length) mappings are in flight at any instant —
INVARIANT   a mapping is "in flight" from the moment gate.open is called until it settles.
INVARIANT every element is mapped exactly once; the result has the same length as the
INVARIANT   input, and result[i] === input[i] * 2 for every i.
INVARIANT an empty input returns an empty array without calling gate.open at all.
